      ":question/id": "fe14c5da-84b9-5f33-afec-8930c586b012",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the fourth row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -9 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -8 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ are in row echelon form.",
